# Trusted gateways for wifi-stealth.zsh (not tracked)
# Install to: /usr/local/etc/wifi-stealth.conf  (root:wheel, 0644)
#
# One "ipv4|mac" pair per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# When this file is absent or empty, no gateway is trusted and stealth
# mode stays on, which is the safe default.
#
# macOS `arp` strips leading zeros from each octet, so a MAC that pfSense
# shows as 08:00:27:0a:1b:2c must be written here as 8:0:27:a:1b:2c.
# Get the current gateway's MAC in the right format with:
#
#   gw=$(route -n get default | awk '/gateway:/ {print $2}'); arp -n "$gw"
#
# Example:
# 192.168.1.1|8:0:27:a:1b:2c
